{"title":"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 48","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_48&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let a and b be relatively prime positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/c/e0c22354f6f8870c3a024305aa3afed00b26bcf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a/b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> is the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/0/cb0591530ee3d7119cf5d52db2ba428e5e870f45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2x_1+\\sin^2x_2+\\sin^2x_3+\\cdots+\\sin^2x_{2007}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"331\" height=\"18\" />, where, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/26363fa4bbe0be5b4869ba7a29aa4e7c061d37eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i\\leq 2007, x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> is a nonnegative real number, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/d/e6d44999d3a8af08fa55202eabf08081c35a768b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1+x_2+x_3+\\cdots+x_{2007}=\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"236\" height=\"13\" />. Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_48&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider a convex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0db9f93bcba529c93ae151a1ac5c740eec7cca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2007$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" />-gon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c72c6dc74d0bb191659e047ebbb99a5f13f92c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1A_2\\cdots A_{2007}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" /> inscribed in a circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddfeb47a9c614ed8d14f5b788585941da72f3b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A_iOA_{i+1} = 2x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" />, with indeces taken mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0db9f93bcba529c93ae151a1ac5c740eec7cca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2007$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" />. Then in particular a quick calculation gives<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/2/952bad6d928875244d25bda01b87aef5b3969b8a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin^2 x_1 + \\cdots + \\sin^2 x_{2007} = A_1A_2^2 + \\cdots + A_{2007}A_1^2.\\]\" width=\"384\" height=\"20\" />It suffices to maximize this sum of squares.\n</p><p>The upshot of this is that it makes the argument that we don't actually need a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0db9f93bcba529c93ae151a1ac5c740eec7cca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2007$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" />-gon somewhat slick. Take such a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0db9f93bcba529c93ae151a1ac5c740eec7cca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2007$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" /> gon. Note that one of the angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598e9cb118f21130c58863b652cf04a2ba89f943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A_{i-1}A_iA_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" /> is non-acute. But then by Law of Cosines<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/f/59f71e5cb8dd3340fd4c83b26348cd87aa0f1818.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A_{i-1}A_{i+1}^2 \\geq A_{i-1}A_i^2 + A_iA_{i-1}^2,\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"21\" />so performing this operation necessarily increases the sum of squares. Repeating this until we have all acute angles necessarily left gives that it suffices to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/7/d475b4c8149849e9b544c4e451f0df242e900662.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB^2 + BC^2 + CA^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is a triangle inscribed in a circle of diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the centroid of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Recall the identity<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5eed4b072fdf490faeb6e1ab2cf4e050deff14b4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PA^2 + PB^2 + PC^2 = 3GP^2 + GA^2 + GB^2 + GC^2\\]\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />which holds for arbitrary points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in the plane. We'll pick points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> that make things nice. First choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/9/0e98e3f69e4bcb1a7f40b69574a0d6312f6c2cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = O$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />; this becomes<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4e7d272cef03a5c4c50ee8725ff1cec7b9f4ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OA^2 + OB^2 + OC^2 = 3GO^2 + GA^2 + GB^2 + GC^2,\\]\" width=\"400\" height=\"19\" />or<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/4/6f4b7675650f690cfd82a63e565270340e27a619.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3R^2 - 3GO^2 = GA^2+GB^2+GC^2.\\]\" width=\"277\" height=\"17\" />Now set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd94b77275e15f426d50513127acaffa0546d244.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> to get the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/2/372dfdd812d524e48841801b7f71ad44b271d1c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB^2 + AC^2 = 4GA^2 + GB^2 + GC^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"286\" height=\"18\" /> Constructing similar equations for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, adding them, and dividing by two yields\\begin{align*}AB^2 + BC^2 + CA^2 &amp;= 3(GA^2 + GB^2 + GC^2) \\\\&amp;= 3(3R^2 - 3GO^2) \\geq 9R^2 = \\boxed{\\tfrac 94}.\\end{align*}Equality holds for an equilateral triangle, which in turn occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/3/5a37167d49a1c9d59348db675d9c0261c5d13722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = x_2 = x_3 = \\tfrac\\pi 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/7625f99ded43984e7ac0bfc740d02a369be2f9fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_4 = x_5 = \\cdots = x_{2007} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"202\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>~ Imported from the Official Solution, given by djmathman\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_48&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest\" title=\"2007 iTest\">2007 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 iTest Answer Key\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_47\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 47\">Problem 47</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_49\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 49\">Problem 49</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Pro